<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Romanov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1613">1613</a>–<a href="/years/1917">1917</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Romanov dynasty, Romanov</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Romanov was the dynasty that ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> from the election of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-of-russia">Michael Romanov</a> as tsar in 1613 until the abdication of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii">Nicholas II</a> in 1917. Descended from a Muscovite boyar family related to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iv-of-russia">Ivan IV</a> through his first wife Anastasia, it produced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a>, and from 1762 the throne passed to its Holstein-Gottorp-Romanov branch. Nicholas II and his family were killed by the Bolsheviks in 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-romanov.jpg" alt="House of Romanov" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Taubiy (original uploader) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:House_of_Romanoff.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
